@startuml
title Medusa — from a failing sequence to a minimal reproduction
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam ArrowColor #4A78B5
skinparam sequence {
  ParticipantBackgroundColor #EEF5FF
  ParticipantBorderColor #4A78B5
  LifeLineBorderColor #4A78B5
  ArrowColor #4A78B5
}

participant "CallSequence\nGenerator" as Gen
participant "FuzzerWorker" as W
participant "TestChain" as C
participant "Test case\nprovider" as P
participant "Execution\ntracer" as T

Gen -> W : base sequence (100 calls)
loop for each call in the sequence
  W -> C : execute call
  C --> W : receipt, logs, revert data
  W -> P : callSequencePostCallTest(sequence)
  P --> W : no failure
end

W -> P : callSequencePostCallTest(sequence)
P --> W : ShrinkCallSequenceRequest\n(+ VerifierFunction)

note over W, P #EEF5FF
The verifier re-checks that the candidate
sequence still triggers the same failure.
end note

loop up to shrinkLimit iterations
  W -> W : drop reverted calls,\nremove one call,\nshrink an argument
  W -> C : replay candidate on a fresh chain
  C --> W : results
  W -> P : verifier(candidate)
  P --> W : still failing / no longer failing
end

W -> C : replay the minimised sequence
W -> T : attach execution tracer
T --> W : annotated trace with console.log output
W -> P : onShrinkResult(minimised sequence)
P --> W : test marked FAILED

@enduml
